WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:10.990
Please don't expect too much from it.
This story is a simple illustration of the three
Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.960
Here, a gift for you guys.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.190
Oh, crackers?

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.760
I thought you might be tired of pudding.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.380
Thank you very much.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.000
I'll put some tea on for you.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.420
Wow, they're really good!

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.830
They're just a little salty!

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:29.890
Yeah, just a little.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.930
If I'd had just a little more courage,

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.710
I'd have been able to
.give these to Reiko-san.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:41.770
Love Now?

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.640
You can have them.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.130
You know how girls like
romance stories, right?

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:51.940
If you're going on a movie date,
.it's got to be a sweet romance flick.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.900
But you see...

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:00.410
The fact that they like romance doesn't mean they'll go with just anyone.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:04.160
In fact, it makes who they see
.it with even more significant.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:10.720
Because they'll spend some sweet time together, bodies so close, in a dark movie theater.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.420
Your tea's going to get cold.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:23.180
Ah, it's just a little bitter!

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:29.900
I thought I'd never love again.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.120
You idiot!

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:42.330
I love you, you idiot!

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.330
Love Now
Love Now

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.000
Now a hit movie!!
The movie that will make you cry your eyes out this fall.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.330
Now playing.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:43.090
Hosaka, it looks like Haruka-chan likes going to the movies.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:43.990
What?!

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.560
I see.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.680
A typical high school date for her would involve the movies.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.750
Her daughters would be
.able to enjoy it with her.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:57.580
So, what kind of movies
does Minami Haruka enjoy?

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.780
I don't know.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.350
But don't people normally see romance flicks on a date?

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.390
I see. Romance.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.140
I hear Love Now has had
.everyone crying lately.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:10.100
Crying...

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.960
Why's this stuff so sweet?

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.960
Popcorn's supposed to be salty! Heretics!

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.880
We're at a movie theater! That makes caramel the norm, you moron!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.940
You're just a kid with a sweet tooth!

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.210
What'd you call me?!

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.870
Wait, Minami Haruka.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.290
I will wipe your tears.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.790
The only thing you
.should wipe is my sweat.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:43.930
Natsuki-kun.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.290
Haruka-senpai?

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.680
Natsuki-kun, do you like movies and stuff?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.350
Movies and stuff?

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.100
Kind of.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.060
Really?

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.520
I got these from someone.
You can have them, if you'd like.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.830
Tickets to a movie?!

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:04.680
I'll go.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.040
Great!

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.240
Think of it as thanks for
.helping at the barbecue.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.250
Bye.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.460
Haruka-senpai is asking me to a movie!

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.710
Love Now?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.440
What kind of movie is it?

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.020
Hitomi!

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.740
Hey, Hitomi, you liked
going to the movies, right?

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:24.970
Well, kind of.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.640
Wanna go see Love Now with me?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.480
What kind of movie was that again?

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.600
It's a romance that's
supposed to make you cry.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.650
<i>That</i> kind of movie?

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.600
A serious romance that makes you cry?

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.050
Wait, hold on, this ticket...

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:44.350
You know the type where little coincidences keep happening and they fall in love?

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.110
I kinda like those kinds of stories, you know?

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.920
Ah. They're not really my kind of thing.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:53.330
Darn. Everyone else said the same.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.150
Guess I'll ask someone else.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.540
Natsuki's eyes... They look as though something kind of sad's happened.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.660
Hey, Natsuki, what's wrong?

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.180
Did something sad happen?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.300
No, nothing like that.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.880
More importantly, Hitomi,

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.840
do you like movies?

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.720
Well, kind of.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.610
Then, if you'd like...

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:17.310
How about it?

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.650
A movie ticket?!

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.380
I'll go.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.100
I see.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:26.860
Good.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.700
What? You got asked to a movie?!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.260
Wh-Wh-Wh-Who?!

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:35.010
It doesn't matter who asked me!

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.700
But look at this!

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:38.440
Love Now!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.370
It's a serious romance, right?

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.500
I did hear that it isn't a
.story you can laugh at.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.980
Whoever's asking you is
.being a little too serious.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:46.630
Wait...

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.640
You had two tickets on top of each other.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.550
Huh? That's weird.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:58.300
When you invite someone to a movie date, you give one to the invitee and keep the other for yourself.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:03.930
She wasn't asked to the movies, she was told to ask someone to the movies.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.480
Oh wait, that's right...

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.120
He had this really sad look in his eyes.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.910
Sad eyes?

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:16.860
Maybe he got these tickets from a girl he liked?

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:17.910
I'm back!

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.650
Oh, Hitomi, you came over?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.460
Thanks for having me.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:27.610
Those crackers are really good,
right? Just a little salty.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:32.100
Kana, didn't Haruka-neesama
have a pair of those tickets too?

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:34.360
Yeah, you're right!

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:37.100
They're just a little salty! They're great!

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.620
Ready?

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.350
Spicy!

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:41.350
Tabasco!

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:44.810
I'm Spicyman!

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.570
Spicy!

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:58.580
What? You haven't asked him out yet?

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:03.880
Look, I'd be asking the person who gave me the tickets to the movie. Awkward much?

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.250
Yeah...

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:11.740
I wonder why he gave me the tickets.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.180
I don't get what guys think.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.080
All right. Let's ask a guy
.what they think, then.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.440
We only have girls here.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:22.730
How about Takeru?

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.220
Let's not ask him.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:25.810
Then...

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:32.950
Thanks for having me.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.270
What did you want to ask me, Minami?

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:36.950
Ah!

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:39.740
Ah!

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:40.330
Huh?

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.400
You two know each other?

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.210
No, it's just...

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.780
When we're rounding corners...

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.120
or buying drinks...

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:55.590
It's that thing where little coincidences keep happening and they fall in love! Love Now!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.320
Sorry, but I'm not interested in younger guys.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.340
I'm not interested in you either!

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:04.800
We won't even need to
.ask Fujioka what guys think.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.440
Coincidentally, we just happen
.to have two movie tickets here.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.720
Naturally, that means you
.two have to go together.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.310
Why do I have to go with her?!
Why do I have to go with him?!

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.600
They're in sync.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.540
Man, they're totally in sync.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.970
Hey, quit copying me!

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:25.580
It's embarrassing!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.180
<i>You</i> quit copying <i>me</i>!

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.540
Come now, you two.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.500
Have some more tea.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.930
They're so in sync,
.it's like a good act.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.140
Yeah.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:38.580
I kind of want to give a
.name to this phenomenon.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:39.970
Yeah, me too.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:40.550
How about "bingo"?

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:41.880
Here you go.
How about "bingo"?

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:41.900
Here you go.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.480
That sounds a bit plain.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.180
Then how about "combo"?

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.980
Hm... Well, we can go with that.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.180
Eight-hit combo!

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.740
That might be a record.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.840
Mind if I use your bathroom?

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:00.480
Another!

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:02.010
Cut it out already!

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:05.740
We only have one bathroom in this
.apartment, so one at a time, please.

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:08.040
All right. Rock, paper, scissors for it.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.380
Fine by me!

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.160
Will we have one?

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.840
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:13.380
There it is!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.340
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:14.880
Whoa!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.820
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:17.060
This is incredible!

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.180
Rock, paper, scissors!
This is incredible!

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.190
Will we have a new record?
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:20.260
Rock, paper, scissors!
Will we have a new record?

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.680
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.720
I can't keep count.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.060
That's gotta be a Guinness World Record.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.560
You can go first.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:31.810
They're so in sync.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.370
What should we do?

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:35.320
They'll never decide at this rate.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:37.200
Quit holding it in and go!

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.770
You don't have the guts for it!

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:41.620
I've got more guts than you!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.580
This is kinda scary...

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:46.580
There's a public restroom
..not too far from here...

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.320
Oh, okay. I can get there in
...two shakes with these legs—

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.080
I can get there in one shake!

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.440
Race you there!

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.960
Hey there...

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:58.970
What the heck?

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.480
We're back!

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.520
So, who won?

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:15.750
It was a tie.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:16.860
Really?

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:20.140
You're pretty good.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.400
You're pretty good too.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:23.700
A blossoming friendship!

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.400
Now if you fall in love,
it'll be just like Love Now!

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:27.820
I told you, not happening!

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:28.620
Love Now?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.890
I really want to see that one.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.300
It's a romance that'll make you
cry your eyes out, right?

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:38.630
I never thought there'd be a girl who'd want
.to see that movie you can't really laugh at.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.480
Coincidentally, we just happen
.to have two tickets right here.

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:43.020
You should go.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:45.050
Hey, those are mine, you know.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:49.490
I was trying to make it so you
.wouldn't have to go alone.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:50.560
Yeah, sure.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:55.410
And anyway, you're supposed to see these romance
.movies as a one-man, one-woman couple on a date.

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:56.060
A date?!

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.440
Is there a girl you like, Fujioka?

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.140
Huh?

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:06.620
Of course he does. Every middle schooler's got one or two.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.410
Why would I have two?

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.040
Then you've got three!

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:17.490
You look like the type that has a hard time
.expressing their feelings to the person they like.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:18.500
Well...

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.020
Y-Yeah...

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.080
Really? Me too.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.210
A combo!

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:25.120
Sucks for us both, huh?

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:26.260
Y-Yeah...

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.760
I bet it does.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:32.720
But!

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:34.820
I believe...

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:37.760
that guys should put forth the effort to express their feelings!

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:41.840
Agreed. I say the guy should do the confessing.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.160
I-I see...

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:52.160
But even if I did, they wouldn't get it...

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.540
Or actually, I already expressed them...

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.140
That means the problem is
.<i>how</i> you expressed them.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:59.090
Definitely how you expressed them.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.960
So, what kind of confession would you want to hear, Hitomi-chan?

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.470
Huh? Me?

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:08.660
Well, let's see...

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:11.760
Fujioka! Listen carefully and take notes!

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:12.760
Okay...

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:16.740
I want him to straight-up say he loves me...

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:23.140
and hold me tight!

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:28.030
Okay. Noted.

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:31.790
Touma...

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.600
She hasn't been doing her chores.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:35.870
And she doesn't listen when I tell her to.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:46.340
How am I supposed to
express my feelings about this?

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.800
Natsuki's eyes...

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.760
He's thinking about how
to express his feelings!

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:54.720
N-Natsuki...

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:58.370
Are you thinking about how
to express your feelings?

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.230
Yeah.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:02.380
Maybe the only way to
.express them is to hit her.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.230
Hit her?!

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:08.360
You're the only person I'll do this to.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.000
That's too intense!
It's just wrong!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:14.680
Really?

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:15.370
Really!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.840
Don't you think you should be a bit gentler?

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.040
Then how would you express your feelings?

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.250
Me?

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.320
I would...

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:32.300
I'm the type to wait until they notice.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.750
Wait?

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.360
You'd just wait?

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:40.350
Um... I'd kinda hover around them, you know?

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:41.810
Hover around them?

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:42.890
Yeah.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.070
What else?

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:48.020
When our eyes meet...

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:55.160
I-I think my feelings would come across.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.660
What if they still don't?

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:05.970
"I love you!"

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:08.740
That's what I'd say.

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:12.960
Huh?

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:16.320
N-No, I've never actually said it...

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.480
That guy...

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:24.020
He's been hovering around for a while now.

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.440
Our eyes met.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:38.340
What? If you've got something to say, then say it!

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:39.870
Listen, Touma.

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:43.880
I lo...

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:45.880
I lo...

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.760
I can't say something like that, damn it!

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.100
What the hell?!

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:59.100
Spicyman
The Spiciest in History!!

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.600
Why do "spicy" and "painful" have to be the same character?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.600
Spicy             Painful
Why do "spicy" and "painful" have to be the same character?

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:03.710
Why do "spicy" and "painful" have to be the same character?

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:18.340
Oh, the pain.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.300
You went to see Love Now on your own?!

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:31.090
What? But it was really
good! I cried so much!

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.010
What's wrong, Riko?

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:44.940
Keiko, how am I supposed
to express my feelings?

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.280
Why not just express them in words?

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:53.580
I'm asking how because I can't do that.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:55.610
Is that a 100 point answer?

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.840
Then why not ask them on a date?

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.580
Oh, Love Now is playing right now.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.480
It's a romance that'll make
you cry! It's really good!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.620
That's way too hard.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:10.590
Good students tend to talk about hard things as though they were the easiest things in the world.

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.400
Th-Then how about giving them a present?

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:18.440
Something handmade might
.express your feelings nicely.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.650
If you come over, I'm sure Keiko'll come too!

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:23.250
A handmade... present?
If you come over, I'm sure Keiko'll come too!

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:24.420
Sure, I'll go.
A handmade... present?

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:24.850
Sure, I'll go.

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:28.060
All right! We're having a
study party later this week!

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.070
Got it, Keiko? Riko?

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.480
Huh?

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:38.300
..A handmade present...
What should I make?

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:40.280
I wonder...

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:45.250
Oh, the girl gave a handmade scarf as a present in Love Now.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.600
A handmade scarf would be
expressing way too many feelings!

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.690
He'll think I'm creepy!

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:53.420
I just brought it up because
...I remembered the movie...

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:56.250
Then how about something sweet?

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:58.580
Once they eat it, it'll be gone forever.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.800
Sweets, huh?

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:03.390
If you make cookies, then when we all get together, you can just open them up and...

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:04.890
Like chocolate?

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.640
No, it's not Valentine's yet.

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:11.760
I could make a cake,
...and we could split it...

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:15.160
No, that'd be too obvious.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:16.530
Oh, I know!

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.120
If I make cookies,

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.280
at least one will get to him!

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.040
All right!

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.600
I'm going to make cookies!

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.520
Later!

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.960
I just said that!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.460
Mukashino                                       Bookstores

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:37.340
I guess following the recipe exactly is the best way to succeed.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:44.820
200 grams of all-purpose flour, 120 grams of unsalted butter, a pinch of salt...

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:47.600
How much is a pinch?

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:49.100
Hey, Keiko!

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:51.720
How much is a pinch?!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:53.640
Just a little?

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:56.460
I'm asking you how much "just a little" is!

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.360
I'm just a little sleepy...

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:02.370
How much is that?!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.890
Man, I'm just a little hungry.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:05.950
How much is that?!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.910
I never knew she was this neurotic...

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:14.200
How much is "just a little"?

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:20.590
Riko, don't you think you're
washing your hands too much?

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:25.140
Right. She can't hear me.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.600
She really is neurotic.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:30.100
What?

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:34.810
Fujioka-kun is crying...

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.540
Oh no! What should I do?

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:38.400
For now, I'll give him my handkerchief—

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:45.830
Oh no! This is my favorite handkerchief that I ironed just this morning, but I already used it!

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:48.830
I can't give him a wet handkerchief...

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.710
What's wrong, Fujioka?

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:51.700
Here, have a handkerchief.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.420
Oh, thanks.

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:58.930
But that's okay. I just got
.a little dust in my eye.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:02.050
Yeah, I know how dust in your eye feels.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:05.010
Shoot.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.920
I was able to refuse her handkerchief,

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:12.520
but I missed out on an opportunity to talk to
Minami tomorrow by washing and returning it!

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:14.500
I'm just a little regretful!

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:15.520
Huh?

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:20.250
Now he looks really depressed...

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.200
I've been just a little sleepy since yesterday.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.980
Guess it's true what they say. "In spring,
..one sleeps a sleep that knows no dawn."

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:33.920
It's fall right now, and late afternoon.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.760
You've got it all wrong, you moron.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.200
Man, now I'm getting really sleepy.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:40.870
Mind if I slept just a little?

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:41.420
Yes.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.680
I was able to make those cookies, but...

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.930
did I put the right amount of salt in?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.390
Maybe I shouldn't pull them out.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:55.780
I smell something just a little
.sweet coming from Riko.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:56.550
Huh?

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:00.320
You mean these?

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.840
They're just a little delicious.

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:14.720
While they're just a little lacking compared to what Haruka-neesama can make,

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:15.830
they're still pretty good.

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:18.510
Don't eat them if you don't like them.

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:26.680
Yeah.

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:29.140
They're good!

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:40.900
I was able to give Fujioka-kun my cookies because they smelled just a little sweet.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:43.540
I'm just a little bit thankful to you, Kana.

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:47.410
If anything, I'd say they need
.just a little more salt.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:48.720
How much is that?!

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:23.250
So you never went to see the movie?

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:27.020
Yeah. It would have stopped playing
before I found the perfect time to go see it.

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:29.130
Next episode: "We Started Living Green."

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:32.160
I hope you don't miss your time for love.

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:32.890
Kana!
